        <mxCell id="fwpolicy" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF6F7;strokeColor=#DD344C;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;fontSize=11;fontColor=#232F3E;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;arcSize=8;" value="&lt;b&gt;Two firewall resources, two policies, shared rule groups.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;An endpoint can only live in its own VPC, so ingress and inspection each need their own firewall. Rule &lt;i&gt;groups&lt;/i&gt; are shared and versioned in git; the &lt;i&gt;policies&lt;/i&gt; differ &amp;#8212; ingress blocks inbound exploits and scans, egress does domain allow/deny, TLS inspection and exfil control.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="52" width="970" x="425" y="958" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tgwcol" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8C4FFF;strokeWidth=3;dashed=0;fontSize=11;fontColor=#232F3E;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;arcSize=8;" value="" vertex="1">
