        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#232F3E;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color: rgb(1, 168, 141);&quot;&gt;Coming in:&lt;/b&gt; user → internet gateway → firewall → load balancer → transit gateway → your app&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b style=&quot;color: rgb(237, 113, 0);&quot;&gt;Going out:&lt;/b&gt; your app → transit gateway → attachment subnet → firewall → NAT → internet gateway → internet&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b style=&quot;color: rgb(231, 21, 123);&quot;&gt;Sideways (east-west):&lt;/b&gt; spoke → TGW → inspection VPC → firewall → &lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;back to the TGW&lt;/b&gt; → the other spoke — it never reaches the NAT gateway&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color: rgb(82, 127, 255);&quot;&gt;Inside the spoke:&lt;/b&gt; application tier → data tier, tcp 5432 / 6379 only — this traffic never leaves the VPC&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b style=&quot;color: rgb(122, 161, 22);&quot;&gt;To AWS services:&lt;/b&gt; application tier → VPC endpoint — straight to AWS, never crosses a firewall&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="161" width="2860" x="50" y="1024" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
